\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Understanding these concepts will help you use AGsInfoFrame effectively:\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b Artistic Groups (AGs)
\f1\b0 : Collections of shapes that share similar hue characteristics. You typically have 4 AGs.\
\
\f0\b Spreads
\f1\b0 : Hue ranges defined for each AG. Each spread has a lower limit, anchor hue, and upper limit.\
\
\f0\b Proportional Location
\f1\b0 : A value (0.0-1.0) that determines where a shape's hue falls within its AG's spread.\
\
\f0\b Fuzzy Logic Phase
\f1\b0 : During initial organization, shapes can be assigned to multiple AGs to explore possibilities.\
\
\f0\b Validation Phase
\f1\b0 : After initial organization, each shape must be in exactly one AG, and hues must be within spreads.\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

